  "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"20\"><mn>20</mn>\n</math>. Adding the first equation to the second equation in the given system yields <math alttext=\"5 y minus 5 y equals 10 x plus 5 x plus 11 minus 21\"><mn>5</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>21</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"0 equals 15 x minus 10\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></math>. Adding <math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math> to both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"10 equals 15 x\"><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mi>x</mi></math>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"20 equals 30 x\"><mn>20</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mi>x</mi></math>. Therefore, the value of <math alttext=\"30 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>30</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"20\"><mn>20</mn>\n</math>.</p>",
